Subject: [PATCH] Account committed guest RAM and deliver memory threshold notifications

Apply in the EKA2L1 root after 0018/0020 (0019 is a separate Dynarmic patch).
Keep the existing per-version emulated RAM totals and allocation behaviour.
Report free RAM from unique non-ROM kernel chunks, not host RAM or guest VA
reservations. Use explicit EKA notification defaults (8/24 MiB), not claimed
firmware settings; the privileged SetMemoryThresholds Exec remains unsupported.

Follow Symbian's strict low/inclusive good crossing, initial change mask and
pending event coalescing. Completion only writes the guest request and wakes
its thread. Reject dead, exited or address-reused requesters and suppress all
completion during kernel teardown. No client callback or GC runs here.

